[00:00.00] I'm watching the clock take the hours away
[00:17.00] For soon I know I'll hang at the dawn of the day
[00:25.00] But why should I fear death when it's life anew
[00:33.00] And dying only brings me much closer to you
[00:42.00] You left me in anger to walk by the sea
[00:50.00] And when they found your body they blamed it on me
[00:59.00] But you know they were wronged here so wait for a while
[01:07.00] For we shall be together beyond the last mile
[01:20.00] The stars hide their face to make way for the sun
[01:40.00] And soon death it shall claim me and make us as one
[01:49.00] While some men are walking the streets with a smile
[01:57.00] Then I know I'll be walking beyond the last mile
[02:07.00] The chaplain is making his last plea to God
[02:15.00] Soon up the numbered steps to the scaffold I'll draw
[02:23.00] My footsteps won't falter I'll walk with a smile
[02:31.00] For I know you'll be waiting beyond the last mile
